            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Criminal</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    [115] The <b>Crown</b>’s submissions on the s. 11(b) issue focus primarily on the <b>transitional</b> exception. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;The <b>Crown</b> urges that the defence was still preparing for the preliminary inquiry and therefore not ready to <b>proceed</b> until October 16, 2013. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[176] The <b>Crown</b> argues this 5.4-month period was all neutral time, not institutional delay, as the parties were not ready to <b>proceed</b> to trial. 
                </p>
