</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/coa/coa/en/item/2964/index.do?q=Crown+Liability+and+Proceedings+Act+section+31+transition">Murray v. Ontario</a></span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2003-08-20</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Civil</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    [3] <b>Sections</b> 27 and 28 of the 1963 <b>Act</b> were re-enacted as ss. 28 and 29 of the 1970 <b>Act</b>. However, ss. 28 and 29 were not included in either the <b>Proceedings</b> Against the <b>Crown</b> <b>Act</b>, R.S.O. 1980, c. 393 (the "1980 <b>Act</b>") or the <b>Proceedings</b> Against the <b>Crown</b> <b>Act</b>, R.S.O. 1990, c. P.27 (the "1990 <b>Act</b>"). &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Section</b> 8 of the Statutes Revision <b>Act</b>, 1989 is to the same effect. [35] I conclude that there is one <b>Proceedings</b> Against the <b>Crown</b> <b>Act</b>, and that the words "under this <b>Act</b>" in s. 28 of the 1970 <b>Act</b> refer to that <b>Act</b>. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[55] <b>Section</b> 3 was first enacted in the <b>Proceedings</b> Against the <b>Crown</b> <b>Act</b>, 1962-63. 
                </p>
