                    The <b>Crown</b> alleged Jun-Chul and Kenneth stole <b>31</b> lottery tickets by pocketing one of the two free tickets won by a customer. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[98] <b>Section</b> 462.37(1) of the Criminal Code authorizes the <b>Crown</b> to seek the forfeiture of any property that is the <b>proceeds</b> of crime, obtained by the commission of a designated offence. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;As a result, the application judge knew that the <b>Crown</b> bore the onus of justifying the delay and the <b>Crown</b> did so on the basis of the <b>transitional</b> exceptional circumstance provision outlined in Jordan. 
