                    Where the court and <b>Crown</b> are ready to <b>proceed</b>, but the defence is not, the defence will have directly caused the delay. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[329] The record does not reveal any occasion on which the court was available, the <b>Crown</b> and co-accused ready to <b>proceed</b> but Kenny was unavailable or not ready to <b>proceed</b>. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;He sought to have the <b>Crown</b> <b>proceed</b> against Kenny on a separate information charging him with manslaughter. 
