        </div> 
    </div> 
    </div> 
</li>
    <li class="odd list-item-expanded">
<div class="number">
    <span class="digits">17.</span>
</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/coa/coa/en/item/5961/index.do?q=Crown+Liability+and+Proceedings+Act+section+31+transition">Wynberg v. Ontario</a></span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2006-07-07</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Civil</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    a) Alleged <b>Section</b> 15 and <b>Section</b> 8(3) Violations para. 204 b) Damages Claim para. 207 &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Section</b> 8(3) of the Education <b>Act</b> requires this. Thus, we agree that they are proper comparators for the purposes of the s. 15(1) analysis. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;However, if the official <b>acts</b> reasonably in the light of the current state of the law and it is only subsequently determined that the action was unconstitutional, there will be no <b>liability</b>. 
                </p>
                <div class="spacer">
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                </div>
        </div> 
        <div class="documents">
