            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    <b>Sections</b> 75(1)(a) and (b) read as follows: <b>Liability</b> of employer on wind up &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;Pension Benefits <b>Act</b>, Regulation 909, R.R.O. 1990, s. <b>31</b>(1), (2) and (3) <b>31</b>. (1) The <b>liability</b> to be funded under <b>section</b> 75 of the <b>Act</b> shall be funded by annual special payments commencing at the effective date of the wind up and made by the employer to the pension fund. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;(a) the amount required in the year to fund the employer’s <b>liabilities</b> under <b>section</b> 75 of the <b>Act</b> in equal payments, payable annually in advance, over not more than five years; and 
                </p>
