</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/coa/coa/en/item/7551/index.do?q=Crown+Liability+and+Proceedings+Act+section+31+transition">St. Jean v. Cheung</a></span>
                        - <span class="citation">2008 ONCA 815</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2008-12-03</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Civil</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    [20] <b>Section</b> 24(2) of the new Limitations <b>Act</b> determines whether the <b>transition</b> provisions in s. 24 apply to a claim based on <b>acts</b> or omissions that took place before January 1, 2004.[5] <b>Section</b> 24(2) reads as follows: &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>SECTION</b> 21 OF THE NEW LIMITATIONS <b>ACT</b> [61] <b>Section</b> 21(1) of the new Limitations <b>Act</b> reads as follows: &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Transition</b> Definitions s. 24. (1) In this <b>section</b>, “effective date” means the day on which this <b>Act</b> comes into force; 
                </p>
                <div class="spacer">
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                </div>
